78141,"to_t":1981.986301369863,"title":"President of Malta","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Anton Buttigieg"},{"qid":"Q233","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q356756","value_label":"Anthony Mamo","from_t":1974.9479452054795,"to_t":1976.9863387978141,"title":"President of Malta","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Anthony Mamo"},{"qid":"Q233","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q57502","value_label":"George Abela","from_t":2009.2547945205479,"to_t":2014.2547945205479,"title":"President of Malta","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"George Abela"},{"qid":"Q233","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q6762928","value_label":"Marie-Louise Coleiro Preca","from_t":2014.2547945205479,"to_t":2019.2547945205479,"title":"President of Malta","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Marie-Louise Coleiro Preca"},{"qid":"Q233","kind":"flag","value_qid":"Q131469","value_label":"Flag of Malta.svg","from_t":1964.72131147541,"to_t":null,"title":"flag of Malta","property":"P163","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"flag of Malta"}],"people":{"Q1647394":{"label":"Myriam Spiteri Debono","description":"11th president of the Republic of Malta","enwiki":"Myriam Spiteri Debono","summary":"Myriam Spiteri Debono (née Zammit; born 25 October 1952) is a Maltese politician who is the 11th and current president of Malta. She is the first Gozitan woman to be elected to the position. She was also the Speaker of the House of Representatives of Malta from 1996 to 1998, the first woman to hold that position.","image":"Myriam Spiteri Debono on April 20, 2024 (cropped).jpg","birth":1952.8142076502731,"death":null},"Q37860840":{"label":"Robert Abela","description":"Maltese politician","enwiki":"Robert Abela","summary":"Robert Abela  (born 7 December 1977) is a Maltese lawyer and politician who has served as prime minister of Malta and leader of the Malta Labour Party since 2020, following the resignation of Joseph Muscat on 13 January that year. The son of former president George Abela, he was elected to Parliament in 2017.","image":"Robert Abela, 2025.06.26 (03) (cropped).jpg","birth":1977.9315068493152,"death":null},"Q1508402":{"label":"George William Vella","description":"Maltese politician","enwiki":"George Vella","summary":"George William Vella  (born 24 April 1942) is a Maltese politician who served as the tenth president of Malta from 2019 to 2024. A member of the Labour Party, he previously served as deputy prime minister of Malta and foreign affairs minister from 1996 to 1998 under prime minister Alfred Sant. In 2013, he returned as foreign affairs minister, an office he held until 2017 under prime minister Joseph Muscat.","image":"Επίσκεψη ΥΠΕΞ Ν. Δένδια στη Μάλτα - Συνάντηση με Πρόεδρο Μάλτας George Vella (10.10.2022) (cropped).jpg","birth":1942.309589041096,"death":null},"Q152511":{"label":"Eddie Fenech Adami","description":"Maltese politician","enwiki":"Eddie Fenech Adami","summary":"Edoardo \"Eddie\" Fenech Adami  (born 7 February 1934) is a Maltese politician and lawyer who served as the prime minister of Malta from 1987 until 1996, and again from 1998 until 2004. Subsequently, he was the seventh president of Malta from 2004 to 2009. He led the Nationalist Party to win four general elections, in 1987, 1992, 1998 and 2003, as well as the majority of votes in 1981. Staunchly pro-European, Fenech Adami was fundamental for Malta's accession to the European Union.","image":"Edward Fenech Adami.jpg","birth":1934.1013698630136,"death":null},"Q167699":{"label":"Ugo Mifsud Bonnici","description":"Maltese politician, activist and writer","enwiki":"Ugo Mifsud Bonnici","summary":"Ugo Mifsud Bonnici,  (born 8 November 1932) is a Maltese politician and was the fifth president of Malta from 1994 to 1999.","image":"Dr Ugo Mifsud Bonnici.jpg","birth":1932.8524590163934,"death":null},"Q167724":{"label":"Guido de Marco","description":"Maltese politician (1931-2010)","enwiki":"Guido de Marco","summary":"Guido de Marco  (22 July 1931 – 12 August 2010) was a Maltese politician, who served as the sixth president of Malta from 1999 to 2004. A noted statesman and lawmaker, de Marco also served as Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of the Interior, Justice, and Minister for Foreign Affairs.\nHe was elected President of the 45th session of the United Nations General Assembly in 1990, and Chairman of the Commonwealth Foundation in 2004. A renowned criminal lawyer, he defended some of the landmark cases in Malta during the 1980s.","image":"Guido de Marco 2003 crop.jpg","birth":1931.5534246575342,"death":2010.6109589041096},"Q167796":{"label":"Paul Xuereb","description":"Acting President of Malta (1923-1994)","enwiki":"Paul Xuereb","summary":"Pawlu \"Paul\" Xuereb (21 July 1923 – 6 September 1994) was a Maltese politician who served as the Speaker of the House of Representatives of Malta from July 1986 to February 1987 and the acting president of Malta from February 1987 to April 1989.\nHe was educated at the Regent Street Polytechnic in London, where he studied journalism, Political Economy and Political Science. Upon completing his studies he returned to Malta in 1950 and took up the post of managing director of Fardex Trade Development Company (Malta) Ltd. In 1958 he joined the Department of Education as a visiting Master at the Lyceum.","image":"Mr Paul Xuereb.jpg","birth":1923.5506849315068,"death":1994.6794520547944},"Q167937":{"label":"Ċensu Tabone","description":"President of Malta (1913-2012)","enwiki":"Ċensu Tabone","summary":"Vincent \"Ċensu\" Tabone,  (Maltese pronunciation: [ˈt͡ʃɛnsʊ tɐˈbɔːnɛ]; 30 March 1913 – 14 March 2012) was the fourth president of Malta who also served as Minister and Nationalist MP.","image":"Dr. Censu Tabone.jpg","birth":1913.2410958904109,"death":2012.1994535519125},"Q168387":{"label":"Agatha Barbara","description":"Maltese politician (1923-2002)","enwiki":"Agatha Barbara","summary":"Agatha Barbara,  (11 March 1923 – 4 February 2002) was a Maltese politician, having served as a Labour Member of Parliament and Minister. She was the first woman to serve as president of Malta, and remains the longest-serving woman Member of Parliament in Maltese political history.","image":"Ms Agatha Barbara.jpg","birth":1923.1890410958904,"death":2002.0931506849315},"Q250177":{"label":"Anton Buttigieg","description":"Maltese politician and poet (1912-1983)","enwiki":"Anton Buttigieg","summary":"Anton Buttigieg  (Maltese: Anton Buttiġieġ [ɐnˈtɔːn bʊtːɪˈd͡ʒɪːt͡ʃ]; 19 February 1912 – 5 May 1983) was a Maltese politician and poet who served as the second president of Malta from 1976 to 1981. Prior to his tenure as president he was a member of the Parliament of Malta and president of the Labour Party.","image":"Dr. Anton Buttigieg.jpg","birth":1912.1338797814208,"death":1983.3397260273973},"Q356756":{"label":"Anthony Mamo","description":"Maltese chief judge and first President of the republic (1909-2008)","enwiki":"Anthony Mamo","summary":"Anthony Joseph Mamo (9 January 1909 – 1 May 2008) was the first president of Malta and before that was the last governor-general of the State of Malta before the country became a republic. He was also the first Maltese citizen to be appointed Governor-General, and before independence, was briefly acting governor.","image":"Sir Anthony Mamo.jpg","birth":1909.021917808219,"death":2008.3306010928961},"Q57502":{"label":"George Abela","description":"Maltese politician (born 1948)","enwiki":"George Abela","summary":"George Abela,  (born 22 April 1948) is a Maltese politician who was the eighth president of Malta from April 2009 to April 2014.","image":"George Abela.jpg","birth":1948.3060109289618,"death":null},"Q6762928":{"label":"Marie-Louise Coleiro Preca","description":"Maltese politician","enwiki":"Marie-Louise Coleiro Preca","summary":"Marie-Louise Coleiro Preca,  (born 7 December 1958) is a Maltese politician who was president of Malta from 2014 to 2019. She has been president of Eurochild since 2019.\nPreviously, as a member of the Labour Party, Coleiro Preca was a Member of Parliament (MP) in the House of Representatives of Malta from 1998 to 2014. She served as the minister for the family and social solidarity from 2013 to 2014 under Prime Minister Joseph Muscat.","image":"Marie-Louise Coleiro Preca (cropped).jpg","birth":1958.9315068493152,"death":null}},"media":{"Flag of Malta.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Flag_of_Malta.svg/330px-Flag_of_Malta.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Malta.svg","author":"See File history below for details.","license":"Public domain"},"Coat of arms of Malta.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Coat_of_arms_of_Malta.svg/330px-Coat_of_arms_of_Malta.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Malta.svg","author":"Tonyjeff, based on national symbol.","license":"Public domain"},"Myriam Spiteri Debono on April 20, 2024 (cropped).jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Myriam_Spiteri_Debono_on_April_20%2C_2024_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Myriam_Spiteri_Debono_on_April_20%2C_2024_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Myriam_Spiteri_Debono_on_April_20,_2024_(cropped).jpg","author":"© European Union 2024 - Source : EP","license":"European Parliament"},"Robert Abela, 2025.06.26 (03) (cropped).jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Robert_Abela%2C_2025.06.26_%2803%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Robert_Abela%2C_2025.06.26_%2803%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Robert_Abela,_2025.06.26_(03)_(cropped).jpg","author":"European Union",